  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ECHO-Accelerating Localisation Through Partnerships-CAFOD contribution</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ECHO has provided funding a 6 member consortium led by Christian Aid (and including CAFOD, ActionAid, Tearfund, Care and Oxfam) to develop and promote local humanitarian leadership capacities in 4 focus countries; South Sudan, Nepal, Nigeria and Myanmar. Consortium members will engage with networks of local and national NGOs, via a consortium/INGO focal point for each respective country, and coordinate a series of workshops and accompaniment programmes to develop and promote the abilities of local humanitarian actors to respond to crises in their unique country settings.
Christian Aid will lead this consortium. CAFOD will contribute towards co-financing of the initiative. We will sit on the project steering committee, support the administration and management of the consortium, and contribute to discussions and implementation at the country level. 
CAFOD is not a focal point agency for any of the 4 countries; as such we will not received any funding in return.</narrative>
  </description>
